      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2002-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factor \\(3x-2\\) out of the first two terms: \\[ \\begin{gathered} (3x-2)(4x+1) \\\\ {}-(3x-2)4x+1 \\\\ {}=(3x-2)(4x+1-4x)+1 \\\\ {}=3x-1. \\end{gathered} \\] At \\(x=4\\) this equals \\(3\\cdot4-1=11.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Group the two terms containing \\(3x-2\\) using the distributive law",
        "\\((3x-2)(4x+1)-(3x-2)4x\\) \\(=(3x-2)(4x+1-4x)\\)"
      ],
